IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Courts Law [Consolidated Version], 5744-1984 (חוק בתי המשפט [נוסח משולב], התשמ״ד–1984), ONLY the provisions Amendment No. 105 touches or the Basic Law cites. Row IL-38, 2026-11-09.
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every other module of this row imports this one.
--
-- SCOPE. Encoded: the provisions Amendment No. 105 touches (ss 2A, 6 with its two definitions, 6B, 6C, 7(b) and (c), 8(a), 25(b)) and two it does not touch: s 2 (which 6C(a) and 25(b) cite) and s 14(b), (c) (the procedure for ending a term under s 7(4) of the Basic Law).
--   Every other section is out of scope: not touched by the amendment and not needed by a provision it touches.
--   The Knesset Law ss 6 and 61 appear only as the targets of cross-references (row IL-38's xrefs module); the indirect amendment of the Knesset Law (No. 53, SH 3389 p. 440 s 7) is not encoded.
-- Sources, deposited under ../../registers/source-bundle/:
--   amending-laws/25_lsr_6165552.pdf  Sefer HaChukim 3389 (1 April 2025) pp. 438-440, Courts Law (Amendment No. 105): AUTHORITATIVE, read from the page images.
--   courts-law-consolidated-version-5744-1984.he.wiki.txt  the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation: an AID, unofficial; it shows both texts, each later one marked "(החל מיום תחילת כהונתה של הכנסת העשרים ושש)".
--
-- SEAT: a candidate for the Supreme Court, a person whom the Knesset might choose as a public representative, and a judge whose term the committee is asked to end.
-- The committee, the Minister, the Knesset and the Court have no seat. Two vintages are explicit inputs and never merged: the text before the 26th Knesset and the text from it.

§ `Nouns of the Courts Law provisions on the Judicial Selection Committee`

DECLARE `A vintage of the Courts Law text` IS ONE OF
    `the text before the 26th Knesset`
    `the text from the 26th Knesset`

-- The facts s 2 asks of a candidate for the Supreme Court.
DECLARE `A candidate for the Supreme Court` HAS
    `years served as a judge of a district court` IS A NUMBER
    `years on the Bar's register or entitled to be, practising in a capacity s 2(2) lists` IS A NUMBER
    `of those years, years in Israel` IS A NUMBER
    `is a distinguished jurist` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Who proposes candidates` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister of Justice`
    `the President of the Supreme Court`
    `members of the committee acting together`

-- Women among the members of each description, for s 6(3A) and (3B).
DECLARE `Women on the committee` HAS
    `women among the Supreme Court justices` IS A NUMBER
    `women among the Government's representatives` IS A NUMBER
    `women among the Knesset's representatives, before the 26th Knesset` IS A NUMBER
    `women among the Bar's representatives, before the 26th Knesset` IS A NUMBER
    `women among the members the coalition Knesset members chose` IS A NUMBER
    `women among the members the opposition Knesset members chose` IS A NUMBER
    `women among the public representatives the Knesset as a whole chose` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `What a provision deals with` IS ONE OF
    `the variations that apply where the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members`
    `the members that are not judges: ministers, Knesset members, public representatives`
    `appointment of a judge on the committee's election`
    `the ordinary decision majority of Basic Law s 4(d)`
    `ending a judge's term by decision of the committee`
    `the eligibility of a Supreme Court judge`
    `the five years' service as a judge of a district court`
    `a Knesset member's secession from a faction`
    `the election of its members to a committee`
    `the Judicial Selection Committee`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing provision` IS A STRING
    `the cited provision` IS A STRING
    `what the citing text says it points at` IS A `What a provision deals with`
    `what the cited provision deals with` IS A `What a provision deals with`
